<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Has-Stack — the composition law

A carrier reads as a ''nameless entity'': essence lives nowhere; identity rides the address; meaning rides what the entity //wears// (its stack) and what its body //says//. Interfaces-and-implements ontology stands REJECTED whole cloth — no carrier //${copula}-a// anything; every carrier //has// things, and the carried things speak for themselves.

TW5 speaks `has` natively: the `tags` field carries the stack, and a tag filter runs the type-predicate. This law governs that field's grammar; `meme` governs copy-shape; `loci` governs the address.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ read the carrier's tags field and title before judging composition; gather which entries resolve, which stand declared-unresolved.
⏿ orient each entry against its definition meme; the carried thing carries the semantics, never the edge.
◇ decide composition posture: which components the carrier wears, which families bound it, which entries await definitions.
▶ author the stack in the meta `tags` field alone; mint missing definition memes where pressure warrants.
↺ verify qualification resolves, family exclusivity holds, no kapu entry rode in ungated; close with unresolved entries named.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! The Seven Clauses

# ''One component, one entity.'' A component exists as exactly one carrier: its definition meme at its `lar:` address — self-describing, self-enacting memetic-wikitext. Shim or pointer tiddlers MUST NOT exist in the corpus at rest; any tag-tiddler a live wiki needs gets derived as `$:/temp` runtime shadow, never synced, never sited.
# ''Short names read as relative addresses.'' Within a carrier scoped `root/@bag/version`, a path-shaped tag qualifies to `lar:///<scope>/<tag>` by derivation (the `loci` office), never by pointer. `lar:` tags pass through qualified; system (`$:/`) and free-form tags ride outside the stack. The meta `tags` field stands as the ''single source'' of the stack; body `#has` edges read as derived residue and burn at normalization.
# ''The mandatory component rides the title.'' Every placed carrier holds exactly one intrinsic: its `lar:` address (`loci` — the transform analog). Everything else composes.
# ''Bare tags read fertile.'' A stack entry whose definition meme has not landed stands ''declared-unresolved'' — a lawful, promotable state, never an error. Promotion follows the rating ladder: bare entry (data-grade) → definition lands (meme) → definition carries law (ano). Open minting, judged by the ladder — never a schema registry. A fixed enum of blessed components in any law reads as the interface sneaking back; refuse it.
# ''Families carry exclusivity.'' Component families (the directory grain) MAY declare arity in their own family meme — "at most one of mine per stack" or "many welcome." Arity semantics live in the carried family, never in the edge.
# ''Kapu rides as a grant.'' A stack entry whose definition wears kapu MUST NOT self-add; the write shore refuses it without the operator's mint. Authority = what a carrier holds and who granted it, never what it //is//.
# ''Dumb edges, smart components.'' The stack edge carries no role vocabulary — no implements, no owns, no defines. Relations beyond composition ride `loulou` (adjacency), `kahea` (live transclusion), `aka` (shadow transclusion) and `pranala` (the anchored pointer); anything richer reifies as a component meme, or a wire entity, that speaks for itself. ''Those sigils carry no role vocabulary either'' — `pranala` keeps one attributed form for the code source-pointer and nothing else — so the ban on role-bearing edges belongs to the edge plane, never to a fence around the stack alone.

Runtime: `qualifyStackTag` / `stackOf` and the `stack` filter operator (`[stack[]]`, `[stack:has[<name>]]`).

